{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective","id":960128,"title":"Why Are Spells Written From A Fallen Perspective, and Not A Supernal Perspective?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-29T17:50:29-07:00","id":960128,"title":"Why Are Spells Written From A Fallen Perspective, and Not A Supernal Perspective?","content":"One premise of the game is that distance is a lie. Distance is not measured in meters, but in emotional separation. In reality, you're closest to whoever and whatever you care about most. But it seem to me that if this is really how things are, and mage spells function according to Supernal Truth, and not Fallen Lie, Space spells should be very different.<br /> <br /> For example, say a mage wanted to cast a spell to see in true distance, and not fallen distance. That would be an unveiling spell, and it would replace his normal senses so that instead of seeing the Fallen Space around him, he sees True Space and its sympathetic distances, where the things that matter most to him are closest. Since he is seeing Space as it truly is, everything around him in Fallen reality would disappear to his senses, and he would instead see a patchwork world of constantly shifting terrain, where places become closer to you as you think about them, and further away as you forget them. He would seem to appear in whichever location he cares about the most, such as the home where he grew up. His family, close friends, and other strong connections would all be right next to him, and his acquaintences and other weaker connections would be farther away. Very weak connections would be off in the distance, and the rest of the world as far as the eye can see would be made of even weaker sympathetic connections, constantly moving and shifting. When he looks at a given person or object or place while under this spell, he wouldn't see where they are in Fallen Reality, or who is with them in Fallen Reality, but he would see them as they are in the present moment. So for example, he could see his best friend's injured body lying next to him, and be able to tell that his friend is hurt, but he wouldn't be able to see anything of the alley his friend is lying in, or the thugs who are kicking him.<br /> <br /> But we've run into a problem. According to the rules, this spell is not just a basic unveiling spell. The game doesn't recognize the existence of a &quot;True Space&quot; that you can just look at with a simple spell. Instead, the game considers this to be tantamount to scrying on every sympathetic connection in creation, all at once, and is therefore impossible. In fact, you can't even try to cast it at Space 1 since you don't have the Sympathy attainment!<br /> <br /> Why the heck can't we cast what should logically be a simple unveiling spell at Space 1? For all the game says about Fallen reality being a &quot;lie&quot;, these Space spells are entirely rooted in it. They're written from a Fallen perspective that sympathetic connections exist divested from Space, as though they didn't even exist. Why don't Space spells function from a perspective of Supernal Truth instead of a perspective of the Fallen Lie?<br /> <br /> This problem applies to all the arcana. Take Time. Arcadia says that Time does not pass in a slow orderly march, the same for everyone. Instead it says that Time is chaotic. It shifts and changes like weather. It slows down, speeds up, reverses, and does all of these things differently for any given person. You would think that Time spells, being rooted in the Supernal Truth of Arcadia, would therefore be chaotic by default, and require extra effort to force them into only the one specific outcome you want. That's not the case. Time spells are instead rooted in the Fallen Lie that Time flows the same for everyone everywhere and never changes, as that is what they default to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:55:20-07:00","id":960131,"title":"","content":"It seems like the Exarchs are doing a good job with controlling the natural laws that guide and rule the &quot;Fallen&quot; world. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T18:16:49-07:00","id":960146,"title":"","content":"Alternatively: All those words about Supernal Truth and Fallen Lie? Just words. Mages don't quite have it right. Just because they can impose some other realities rules, doesn't mean they know it all. The phenomena you just brought up maybe be evidence of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T18:28:46-07:00","id":960153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960131#post960131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like the Exarchs are doing a good job with controlling the natural laws that guide and rule the &quot;Fallen&quot; world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess what really prompted this is seeing how interesting the game could be if this weren't the case. KULT, another gnostic themed RPG, is all about the idea that the Lie is breaking, and one wrong step can show you how utterly bizarre the world really is. For example, in Mage, time flows the same because the mystic forces of the universe that you can never see make it so. In Kult, time flows the same because people's clocks and watches are actually slimy parasites that inject them with a drug that makes time flow normally. In KULT, the exarch equivalents don't just invisibly magic their problems away,or have a Seer magic the problems away, they have thousands and thousands of minor servants disguised as people who go around reinforcing the Lie, patching up irises to various other dimensions, and dealing with anyone who's seen too much.<br /> <br /> I think it would be more interesting if more of the game's setting were something you could visit and explore, and not something you're just informed of. For example, Mind is the one arcanum where this problem doesn't exist. The Lie says that no person can truly understand anyone else, because all minds are separate. Mind says that all minds are connected, and that hurting one person is the same as hurting yourself, because all minds are one. That's evident from the Astral Realms, and the Astral realms are a major selling point of the game. I think it would be cool if the other arcana followed a similar concept where you could find physical evidence that the Lie is false, and actually visit the corresponding Supernal Truth first-hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-29-2016, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T18:55:12-07:00","id":960163,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...interesting. Definitely something to think about. <br /> <br /> It seems both bizarre and normal at the same time. Ooohh...this could totally be a 4 base opacity mystery for my mystagogue Mastigos! Thanks Strill! \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T19:29:24-07:00","id":960173,"title":"","content":"Nothing prevents you of portraying Mastigoi Mage Sight in such a fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T19:49:38-07:00","id":960183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960173#post960173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing prevents you of portraying Mastigoi Mage Sight in such a fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules prevent me, because portraying the world in this way leads to rules exploits since the game wasn't designed to account for this perspective. For example, if &quot;True Space&quot; exists, then looking at your friend through True Space is the same as being in sensory range. After all, True Space is a physical place, and it's more real than Fallen Space as well. So then by looking through True Space, you should be able to bypass Sympathy requirements and cast sensory range spells on all your sympathetic connections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T20:02:10-07:00","id":960186,"title":"","content":"All Supernal &quot;Laws&quot; have to be super imposed over the Fallen ones creating a conflict of interests that the Mage has to struggle against (Basic Lie induced knowledge vs. Supernal insight gained via experience). Dots in arcana imply an overcoming of this conflict allowing greater ease in imposing the Supernal truths that the Mage understands. That being said, Scrying really ought to be Unveiling in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Also, if you actually read the rules for Sympathy you'd see that you are in fact casting Sensory Range spells on your sympathetic connections. Pg. 193","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T20:34:39-07:00","id":960198,"title":"","content":"Because Mages are Fallen.<br /> <br /> Problem solved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T20:40:44-07:00","id":960204,"title":"","content":"This. Mages are natives to the Fallen World, who have the ability to tap into the Supernal World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T20:57:32-07:00","id":960210,"title":"","content":"More on point- <i>players </i>are Fallen.<br /> <br /> Like, I love Supernal impossibilities as much as anyone, and I'm apparently one of the rare few who <i>gets</i> the Time Arcanum, but at the end of the day, Jo and Cledus need to be able to parse the shit you're talking about it or the book isn't much use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T21:28:41-07:00","id":960223,"title":"","content":"Gnosis isn't an on/off switch. Neither is Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Mages learn. You're describing the difference between a theory and a practice. &quot;Distance is a Lie&quot; is a theory at Space 1, not a Practice.<br /> <br /> Spells aren't superpowers. They're prototypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T22:51:14-07:00","id":960249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960210#post960210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More on point- <i>players </i>are Fallen.<br /> <br /> Like, I love Supernal impossibilities as much as anyone, and I'm apparently one of the rare few who <i>gets</i> the Time Arcanum, but at the end of the day, Jo and Cledus need to be able to parse the shit you're talking about it or the book isn't much use.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral Realms do this well enough for Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T00:17:24-07:00","id":960274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960249#post960249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Astral Realms do this well enough for Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet at the same time they are very strange. It takes time to grok the strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T00:27:16-07:00","id":960276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960146#post960146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively: All those words about Supernal Truth and Fallen Lie? Just words. Mages don't quite have it right. Just because they can impose some other realities rules, doesn't mean they know it all. The phenomena you just brought up maybe be evidence of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternative 2: <b>Supernal Magic is <i>just</i> supernatural madness spreading by Awakened themselves.</b> There are no Supernal Realms, it just mass hysteria mages are saying too themselves is 'Perfect Reality'. Supernal Beings are just constructs of Awakened will that touch on common symbols of 'magic' sorcerers grow with ( Angels, Demons, Fae, etc. )<br /> <br /> \u200bThere is only 'Fallen Reality' and madness of mages...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T02:19:32-07:00","id":960310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960249#post960249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Astral Realms do this well enough for Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it does, first of all Oneiros are separate. There's a connection between humans to humanity via the Temenos but that isn't the same as saying all minds are one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T05:00:46-07:00","id":960358,"title":"","content":"very interesting perspective. i like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T05:17:33-07:00","id":960370,"title":"","content":"This is how Abyss comes into play. If mages Ascended then they free themselves from the Lie. Anything but Ascension is accepting at least some Exarch influence, since mages are still grounded into their Fallen world.<br /> <br /> That perspective of the Arcana might be an excelent discription of an Awakening and how a mage became obssessed with discovering the Truth (Archmastery) of Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:31:34-07:00","id":960530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960153#post960153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, in Mage, time flows the same because the mystic forces of the universe that you can never see make it so. In Kult, time flows the same because people's clocks and watches are actually slimy parasites that inject them with a drug that makes time flow normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T11:09:15-07:00","id":960554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960198#post960198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Mages are Fallen.<br /> <br /> Problem solved.</div> </div> </div> </div>This,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960223#post960223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gnosis isn't an on/off switch. Neither is Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Mages learn. You're describing the difference between a theory and a practice. &amp;quot;Distance is a Lie&amp;quot; is a theory at Space 1, not a Practice.<br /> <br /> Spells aren't superpowers. They're prototypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this.<br /> <br /> There's a difference between knowing that space is a Lie, and being able to actually see the truth. Mages are still trapped within a reality that they know is a Lie, but can only see through in small glimpses. Gnosis represents how well you grok the truths that you know, and Arcana represent your ability to use that understanding to change your reality. What you describe as a Space Unveiling spell is closer to what Ascended Mages see. A Fallen Mage can only see small glimpses of that ultimate truth at a time, such as by Scrying. Awakening only shows you a brief moment of Truth, it doesn't completely free you from the Lie. Only Ascension can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T12:39:07-07:00","id":960609,"title":"","content":"The comparison to Kult is kinda off. Elysium and the Lie are only superficially similiar concepts. Elysium is literally a false world projected over reality. The Lie is about the platonic underpinnings of reality being warped so that people can't percieve that platonic realm. Those aren't the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T12:54:15-07:00","id":960618,"title":"","content":"This topic makes me think of the Shadow Police series (better known as London Falling + sequels) where one charachter knows how to get to, for lack of a better world, astral realms. But it requires more and more danger each time. He goes there when he's stuck trying to solve the plot's mystery and gets a hint from whatever god happens to be around.<br /> <br /> Given that this system is almost a metaphor for a junkie doing more and more to get his fix, just add addiction (to mystery), it could fit well in Mage and be adapted as a way to see through the Lie in small bursts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:01:13-07:00","id":960623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960609#post960609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comparison to Kult is kinda off. Elysium and the Lie are only superficially similiar concepts. Elysium is literally a false world projected over reality. The Lie is about the platonic underpinnings of reality being warped so that people can't percieve that platonic realm. Those aren't the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right. The key difference is that in KULT, the players are (mostly) mortals. Hence, the false world is something more physical that they can interact with. With mages, the Lie is far more abstract, but their powers are also more abstract. In other words, the end result should be the same in both games - the player characters can see through and interact with the the Lie. I think that when the game interprets the Lie in a way that players can see, explore, and interact with, it makes the game much more interesting than when the Lie is simply an invisible force.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason they changed Mage Sight in Mage 2.0. Not being able to interact with the Supernal realms was no fun. I'm taking a similar approach to the Lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960554#post960554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between knowing that space is a Lie, and being able to actually see the truth. Mages are still trapped within a reality that they know is a Lie, but can only see through in small glimpses. Gnosis represents how well you grok the truths that you know, and Arcana represent your ability to use that understanding to change your reality. What you describe as a Space Unveiling spell is closer to what Ascended Mages see. A Fallen Mage can only see small glimpses of that ultimate truth at a time, such as by Scrying. Awakening only shows you a brief moment of Truth, it doesn't completely free you from the Lie. Only Ascension can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then where does Mage Sight fit into this? I would expect it to simply be the mage seeing through the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-30-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:20:57-07:00","id":960635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960623#post960623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm taking a similar approach to the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. You've presented a highly abstract issue with nothing even vaguely like a solution. Frankly on the back of all the other threads, I'm not sure what you were expecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:38:24-07:00","id":960642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960623#post960623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then where does Mage Sight fit into this? I would expect it to simply be the mage seeing through the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Mage Sight is seeing the Supernal symbols that underly Fallen reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:46:09-07:00","id":960649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960635#post960635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly. You've presented a highly abstract issue with nothing even vaguely like a solution. Frankly on the back of all the other threads, I'm not sure what you were expecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The solution is that these things be portrayed as less &quot;invisible law of the universe&quot; and more something that you can see and interact with.<br /> <br /> Take the fact that Time is stable, but Arcadia says it's chaotic. My approach would be to say that Time IS chaotic, even in the Fallen World. Mages can see and document natural Time eddies and storms. Time sight can see constant minor variations in the flow of Time. These Time storms cause deja vu, make people unexpectedly late, and sometimes cause unexplained disappearances. Now let's say there's some mundane object or action that interacts with Time, quelling disruptions in time. This deserves more thought, but for the sake of expediency, I'll say wood. The grains in wood somehow are able to stabilize Time's natural fluctuations.<br /> <br /> With these changes, the Lie is now something that mages can interact with and study. It becomes a plot point and a story hook. Giving Time something physical to interact with makes it less abstract, more tangible, easier to grok, and pushes it away from being a deus ex machina. The players can investigate the time-affecting properties of wood, and perhaps find that these properties are somehow artificial, giving them evidence that stable time is part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960642#post960642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Mage Sight is seeing the Supernal symbols that underly Fallen reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those Supernal symbols are called the &quot;Truth&quot; because they are in direct opposition to the &quot;Lie&quot;. Hence, why I say that a Mage sees through the Lie using Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960310#post960310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it does, first of all Oneiros are separate. There's a connection between humans to humanity via the Temenos but that isn't the same as saying all minds are one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I understand it, Mages argue that Oneiroi are all a part of the Temenos, and that their rigid separation is part of the Lie. Regardless, the fact that the Astral Realms are a place you can visit is great because it lets players explore and study the Lie. They can visit the boundary between Oneiros and Temenos, and search for signs of artificiality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-30-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:58:42-07:00","id":960655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960649#post960649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And those Supernal symbols are called the &quot;Truth&quot; because they are in direct opposition to the &quot;Lie&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Mages call the state of reality under the Exarchs &quot;the Lie&quot; because it hides the deeper Truth that they perceive as the Supernal through the overlay of Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> The unAscended don't look at the Truth save through metaphor, which is necessarily filtered through the context of the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960649#post960649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I understand it, Mages argue that Oneiroi are all a part of the Temenos, and that their rigid separation is part of the Lie. Regardless, the fact that the Astral Realms are a place you can visit is great because it lets players explore and study the Lie. They can visit the boundary between Oneiros and Temenos, and search for signs of artificiality.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a rigid separation between <i>the Temenos and the Anima Mundi</i>. That's a thing that could conceivably be related to the world's Fallen state, but it's got buggerall to do with the illusion that there is no unity to the qualities of the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-30-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:25:56-07:00","id":960676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960655#post960655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Mages call the state of reality under the Exarchs &quot;the Lie&quot; because it hides the deeper Truth that they perceive as the Supernal through the overlay of Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> The unAscended don't look at the Truth save through metaphor, which is necessarily filtered through the context of the Fallen World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. so Mage Sight IS a mage seeing through the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:33:30-07:00","id":960684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960676#post960676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. so Mage Sight IS a mage seeing through the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's seeing the Truth hidden in reality.<br /> <br /> Seeing through the Lie is <i>Awakening.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:56:59-07:00","id":960692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960655#post960655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a rigid separation between <i>the Temenos and the Anima Mundi</i>. That's a thing that could conceivably be related to the world's Fallen state, but it's got buggerall to do with the illusion that there is no unity to the qualities of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't catch your meaning. You think that humanity's separation from the world is indicative of it being Fallen? I don't know what you mean by &quot;unity to the qualities of the universe&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:07:05-07:00","id":960698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960692#post960692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't catch your meaning. You think that humanity's separation from the world is indicative of it being Fallen? I don't know what you mean by &quot;unity to the qualities of the universe&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that there being a big fuck-off rock in the Astral cutting off the soul of humanity from the soul of the world is a thing that wasn't the case in the Time Before \u2014 we have no way to tell by virtue of the way Supernal reality-edits work \u2014 but there is no presented in-universe argument that the thinner barrier between the soul of humanity and individual human souls has any bearing on the ways the Exarchs supposedly altered the universe to trap mankind in spiritual infancy and keep them from Awakening.<br /> <br /> The notion that all Space is one point (and likewise for the rest of the Arcana through the definitional sympathy of the Supernal) is marginally easier to grasp by looking at the Astral, wherein all navigation relies on working through neighboring concepts, but Mage Sight is not looking at the Supernal in the ostensible apex of that notion where all things are one thing and piercing the veils of individuation is trivial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:48:00-07:00","id":960718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960698#post960698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be that there being a big fuck-off rock in the Astral cutting off the soul of humanity from the soul of the world is a thing that wasn't the case in the Time Before \u2014 we have no way to tell by virtue of the way Supernal reality-edits work</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't we? We know that Supernal reality edits are never perfect. They leave behind fragments of past realities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2014 but there is no presented in-universe argument that the thinner barrier between the soul of humanity and individual human souls has any bearing on the ways the Exarchs supposedly altered the universe to trap mankind in spiritual infancy and keep them from Awakening. </div> </div> </div>That may be true, but separating human minds does seem like something the Exarchs would do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The notion that all Space is one point (and likewise for the rest of the Arcana through the definitional sympathy of the Supernal) is marginally easier to grasp by looking at the Astral, wherein all navigation relies on working through neighboring concepts, but Mage Sight is not looking at the Supernal in the ostensible apex of that notion where all things are one thing and piercing the veils of individuation is trivial. </div> </div> </div>I wasn't suggesting in the OP that a mage could see all of reality condensed into a single point. I was suggesting that a mage could look at Sympathy as though it were a dimension like height or width, and in doing so, change their perception of the world. The fact that Sympathy is invisible to all but mages is part of the Lie because it's a fundamental aspect of reality that's seemingly been sealed off to seem as though it didn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:53:50-07:00","id":960722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960676#post960676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. so Mage Sight IS a mage seeing through the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like looking thru a keyhole. It's not the whole picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T16:03:42-07:00","id":960728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960718#post960718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't we? We know that Supernal reality edits are never perfect. They leave behind fragments of past realities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same process also lets in bits of unreality that cannot be and never were, and it's<i> iterative</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that Sympathy is invisible to all but mages is part of the Lie because it's a fundamental aspect of reality that's seemingly been sealed off to seem as though it didn't exist. </div> </div> </div>Sympathy <i>isn't</i> invisible. &quot;Things are connected to other things that they are like or have touched&quot; is a normal facet of reality that happens to have a massive amount of supernatural significance.<br /> <br /> The tendency of Sleepers to ignore the omens that pervade their surroundings is part of the Lie; the Lie does not make sympathy seemingly nonexistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-30-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T16:14:50-07:00","id":960731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960728#post960728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy <i>isn't</i> invisible. &quot;Things are connected to other things that they are like or have touched&quot; is a normal facet of reality that happens to have a massive amount of supernatural significance.<br /> <br /> The tendency of Sleepers to ignore the omens that pervade their surroundings is part of the Lie; the Lie does not make sympathy seemingly nonexistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't invisible? As far as I'm aware, mages can't detect it without Space Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T16:30:27-07:00","id":960736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960731#post960731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't invisible? As far as I'm aware, mages can't detect it without Space Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathy is more than the connections that the Sympathetic Range Attainment interfaces with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T17:36:24-07:00","id":960756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960731#post960731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't invisible? As far as I'm aware, mages can't detect it without Space Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said, but even if it is only visible with MS, or other spells, so what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:05:44-07:00","id":960772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960736#post960736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sympathy is more than the connections that the Sympathetic Range Attainment interfaces with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? And what else does it cover? The Mage 1.0 Corebook mentions &quot;Like Attracts Like&quot;, but as far as I'm aware, this was never elaborated on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960756#post960756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said, but even if it is only visible with MS, or other spells, so what?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was pointing out that it's part of the Lie because it's a universal law of reality, yet its effects are completely hidden as though it didn't exist, to the point where only spells can reveal it. It suggests that it's something that was purposefully hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:24:05-07:00","id":960777,"title":"","content":"Sympathetic connections are not the things themselves. When you use Space to see sympathetic connections, you see threads, the Literal connections of sympathy, not the things connected. Otherwise you would see nearly everything (except for the rare Psychonaut/paranoid mage that has severed all of their connections), and that's just ridiculous.<br /> <br /> This is a game about magic as presented to people that don't have these kind of abilities. There's always limitations, especially since these mages are NOT living in the Supernal realms. Fallen reality exists and mages still have to live in it and deal with it's laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:09:18-07:00","id":960800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960676#post960676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. so Mage Sight IS a mage seeing through the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Mage Sight shows the Mage the symbols that reality is an imperfect reflection of. Going back to the Space example, &quot;Space Sight allows the user to instantly judge distances, range bands, and cover, allowing the player to know what bonuses or penalties would be in effect before the character acts. It also detects spatial warps, scrying windows, and the presence of Irises.&quot; (Page 91). It shows the Mage symbols that describe those distances.<br /> <br /> What reveals to a Mage the truth that distance is a Lie and all things are in the same place, connected by sympathy and separated only by artificial boundaries they impose on themselves is <i>Awakening to the Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet</i>. &quot;To a Mastigos, the world shows how all thinking minds turn back on themselves, and how illusionary separation and distance is. Warlocks experience warping distance, mirages, and feelings of being lost, watched, or chased. Thinking beings are surrounded by indistinct <i>auras</i>, wrapped in their own thoughts and emotions. Under Focused Mage Sight, many Mastigos sense chains, bars, uniforms, or other representations of imposed boundaries.&quot; (Page 65).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:20:31-07:00","id":960804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960728#post960728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same process also lets in bits of unreality that cannot be and never were, and it's<i> iterative</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a minute. My understanding was that bits of the Time Before still exist because their supernal symbols haven't been destroyed, only overwritten. You're saying it's because they're actually pieces of the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:33:41-07:00","id":960808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960772#post960772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? And what else does it cover? The Mage 1.0 Corebook mentions &amp;quot;Like Attracts Like&amp;quot;, but as far as I'm aware, this was never elaborated on.<br /> <br /> I was pointing out that it's part of the Lie because it's a universal law of reality, yet its effects are completely hidden as though it didn't exist, to the point where only spells can reveal it. It suggests that it's something that was purposefully hidden.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have this tendency to continue to rely on 1e erroneously.<br /> <br /> That being said so what if it does appear as a truth that's completely hidden without MS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:51:09-07:00","id":960813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960772#post960772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? And what else does it cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way signing your name on a Watchtower gives you the beginnings of awareness and influence over the Supernal.<br /> <br /> The way Resonance works with regards to spirits, goetia, ley lines, Avernian Gates, and other similar phenomena.<br /> <br /> The way the Temenos and the Oneiros sort themselves by theme and mood.<br /> <br /> The way vampires and Prometheans can detect each other.<br /> <br /> The way half the Begotten powerset works.<br /> <br /> I could go on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960804#post960804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a minute. My understanding was that bits of the Time Before still exist because their supernal symbols haven't been destroyed, only overwritten. You're saying it's because they're actually pieces of the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I am not.<br /> <br /> A sewage main bursting into my tank of mineral water does not make the minerals in that water into sewage, but it certainly doesn't make me more eager to drink from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-30-2016, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:51:13-07:00","id":960815,"title":"","content":"Isn't <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> going to be introducing Chains and the Labyrinth as features of Mastigos Mage Sight? From the Mastigos preview: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Iron Maze: Pandemonium in the Lie</span></b><br /> Warlocks know that the Supernal lies within, so one never truly leaves Pandemonium, but becomes aware of its presence the Lie. Mastigos see the <i>Labyrinth</i> that describes the world better than any map. Tear away false dimensions, and the cosmos is a maze of sympathetic connections, seen as tunnels, dystopian streets or paths in a decrepit wood. Love, hate, history and mystic resonances mark the true distance between two points. The Labyrinth is the mind as well: corridors in a museum of memory of symbolism. The maze of self and world gives a traveler free passage, but we all experience the bondage of self-doubt and delusion: the <i>Chains</i> that bind us to thought patterns, or shackle locations in Space. Mastigos who strongly prefer the Psychonaut aspect of the Path call themselves wanderers of the Labyrinth. Ardent Warlocks typically master the Chains, breaking or forging them in magical imago. Most Mastigos visualize both signs and combine them with personal imagery.</span></div><br /> These &quot;[Realm] in the Lie&quot; sections didn't make it into <b>Mage 2e</b>; but in his overview of <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>, Dave mentioned that they'd be making an appearance there. Hopefully, they'll do so in a more detailed way than this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-30-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:23:35-07:00","id":960856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960815#post960815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> going to be introducing Chains and the Labyrinth as features of Mastigos Mage Sight? From the Mastigos preview:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Iron Maze: Pandemonium in the Lie</span></b><br /> Warlocks know that the Supernal lies within, so one never truly leaves Pandemonium, but becomes aware of its presence the Lie. Mastigos see the <i>Labyrinth</i> that describes the world better than any map. Tear away false dimensions, and the cosmos is a maze of sympathetic connections, seen as tunnels, dystopian streets or paths in a decrepit wood. Love, hate, history and mystic resonances mark the true distance between two points. The Labyrinth is the mind as well: corridors in a museum of memory of symbolism. The maze of self and world gives a traveler free passage, but we all experience the bondage of self-doubt and delusion: the <i>Chains</i> that bind us to thought patterns, or shackle locations in Space. Mastigos who strongly prefer the Psychonaut aspect of the Path call themselves wanderers of the Labyrinth. Ardent Warlocks typically master the Chains, breaking or forging them in magical imago. Most Mastigos visualize both signs and combine them with personal imagery.</span></div>These &quot;[Realm] in the Lie&quot; sections didn't make it into <b>Mage 2e</b>; but in his overview of <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>, Dave mentioned that they'd be making an appearance there. Hopefully, they'll do so in a more detailed way than this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually what I'm hoping Dave will spoil next. It's also probably the part I'm most looking forward to in Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> And, of course, relevant to this thread. Greater detail on how a Mastigos sees Space would definitely shed light on the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:27:07-07:00","id":960862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960813#post960813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way signing your name on a Watchtower gives you the beginnings of awareness and influence over the Supernal.<br /> <br /> The way Resonance works with regards to spirits, goetia, ley lines, Avernian Gates, and other similar phenomena.<br /> <br /> The way the Temenos and the Oneiros sort themselves by theme and mood.<br /> <br /> The way vampires and Prometheans can detect each other.<br /> <br /> The way half the Begotten powerset works.<br /> <br /> I could go on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that this is applicable in all contexts. You're also saying that it's perfectly evident to a sleepwalker who studies it, but not to sleepers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I am not.<br /> <br /> A sewage main bursting into my tank of mineral water does not make the minerals in that water into sewage, but it certainly doesn't make me more eager to drink from it. </div> </div> </div>I'm not following you at all. How does the Abyss relate to the Time Before?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960808#post960808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have this tendency to continue to rely on 1e erroneously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm grasping at straws here. You're not explaining what you meant, so I posted the only relevant bit of lore I could think of to try and guess your meaning. I'm sorry it wasn't up to your standards. Reading Satchel's post, however, it looks like that bit from 1st edition was indeed relevant and correct, so I don't know what you're getting so critical about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said so what if it does appear as a truth that's completely hidden without MS? </div> </div> </div>Then that suggests that someone hid it, probably the Exarchs. <br /> <br /> It also suggests that it's difficult to convey to players without getting into a bunch of navel gazing that you can't really describe in any tangible sense. I find that less engaging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960815#post960815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These &quot;[Realm] in the Lie&quot; sections didn't make it into <b>Mage 2e</b>; but in his overview of <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>, Dave mentioned that they'd be making an appearance there. Hopefully, they'll do so in a more detailed way than this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonderful! This is perfect. Giving sympathetic connections a metaphor like this seems like it'll make them a lot more tangible, relevant, and easier to approach. Less vague abstract navel gazing and more touching stuff and exploring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T22:10:01-07:00","id":960881,"title":"","content":"There's actually a pretty significant difference between &quot;Space practitioner&quot; and &quot;Mastigos&quot;, too. A Path is a lot more than just a pair of Arcana, which is why a Thyrsus sees Space differently from a Moros. An Obrimos would probably see sympathy in terms of a taxonomy of similarities, whereas an Acanthus would probably see sympathy as a window of opportunity. This is why the Moros and Obrimos perspectives of the Death Arcanum are completely at odds.<br /> <br /> I've been finding the Path descriptions somewhat inadequate and have been working on (okay, it's been a month since I last worked on it) a clearer, more technical explanation of each as opposed to the poetic style in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T22:39:06-07:00","id":960889,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> said. In particular, Chains and Labyrinths are a Mastigos thing, the same way Imps and Wraiths are. An Acanthus who adds Space to her Mage Sight isn't going to see Labyrinths; she'll see something suitable to Arcadia's view of Space. What that is, I don't know yet; and it's a perfect example of why I hope <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> goes into more detail than the examples from the Path Previews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:49:04-07:00","id":960918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960862#post960862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying that this is applicable in all contexts. You're also saying that it's perfectly evident to a sleepwalker who studies it, but not to sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be frank, yes. It's a facet of occult principles based in part on the human tendency to correlate things by proximity and similarity. Shockingly, sympathy has a relation to Blood Sympathy and like-calls-to-like is part of the basis of Azoth Calls To Azoth and this is an observable trend in supernatural metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Things imply other things. Shared qualities aren't inherently invisible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not following you at all. How does the Abyss relate to the Time Before? </div> </div> </div>When the process that fails to completely erase traces of the original state of the world also lets in meaning-destroying cosmic falsehoods every other time it happens and this process has happened multiple times with some regularity since approximately the dawn of existence as we know it, &quot;the process isn't perfect&quot; says <i>absolutely nothing useful</i> as a response to &quot;the way the process works means it's basically impossible to ascertain the original state of the world with any certainty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T01:03:57-07:00","id":960937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960128-why-are-spells-written-from-a-fallen-perspective-and-not-a-supernal-perspective?p=960889#post960889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Acanthus who adds Space to her Mage Sight isn't going to see Labyrinths; she'll see something suitable to Arcadia's view of Space. What that is, I don't know yet;</div> </div> </div> </div>My best guess is &quot;opportunities&quot;. The Acanthus Path is all about agency and taking control of your own destiny. And Space, in those terms, is about the openings in fate during which you can do that. <i>When</i> and <i>where</i> do you grab those opportunities? When do they present themselves? Where are you in life when they show up? A weak sympathetic connection is a lost opportunity, a chance you didn't take, a door you've let close. A strong sympathetic connection is more than a crossroads; it's a hub of possibility, with infinite branches down which your story might go, at this exact moment in time. It's the green at the center of town; it's the Rome to which all roads lead.<br /> <br /> Warlocks see Labyrinths because they're all about confrontation, about testing things by seeing if they break when bent. About taking a wall and turning it into a bridge and saying there is no separation, not really, it's just a matter of understanding how two things relate and aren't really different after all. So the Labyrinth is a metaphor for how people have put up walls: that Truth they see is the Truth of the Lie. Which is funny because it's paradoxical but hey, all Supernal truth is like that when you really think about it, which suggests that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> back there on page 1 has a really good point.<br /> <br /> Scrying, to a Witch, is the answer to, &quot;If only I could see him!&quot; To a Warlock, it is the answer to, &quot;I'm not supposed to see him.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}